  "findings": [
    "Natural formation works on this network. Each run that met the gate formed 3 to 6 trains from ordinary demand and dispatch, and all per-tick checks of the test pass.",
    "A third pod behind the pair is still the main refusal: it ends 193 of the 230 approaches in the five recorded runs. The reservation claims the assembly lane from its first cell, and the next spoke pod takes that cell, its From node, or the junction of p while the pair waits for the junction of M.",
    "After the reservation plan passed, the adoption preparation refused 7 approaches with \"motion start is not representable on its distance grid\" and 2 with \"actual continuation cannot close joint release and stopping room\". These are refusals before a train exists, not faults. This record does not diagnose them.",
    "A pair that shares a branch can link on the approach lane with no turn, when the fork lane starts more than platoonHorizon (300 m) ahead. prepareCouplingApproach then accepts the pair, and a later check refuses it.",
    "Mixed occupancy and pending pickups refuse many pairs at rest, because the fleet is saturated and many spoke pods are empty on the way to a pickup.",
    "Approaches that wait in the grant phase for the slow crossing cost most of the simulation time: planNativeCouplingTick takes about 60% of the CPU time of a run."
